TITLE='Authentic title "The Biggest Wealth Killers in Your 20s and 30s (AVOID At All Costs)" is a list-warning frame with an age target. The script delivers six named killers (lifestyle creep, cars, card debt and BNPL, waiting, no emergency fund, looking rich and overtrading) through the Maya/Dylan roommate story, so the promise is honoured; the count is not stated in the title.'
THUMB='Registered maxresdefault 1280x720 (HTTP 200, real image). White field. Left: the recurring cartoon man, arms crossed, frowning. Top: black headline "PLEASE NOT BUY" (ungrammatical, with BUY larger). Centre: a beige pickup truck in flames with red glow; around it a black "PREMIUM CARD" credit card, a two-tone luxury watch, and a black "PREMIUM CLOTHING" shopping bag. At 320x180 the headline stays legible; the burning truck reads clearly; the card and bag labels become illegible. The burning truck matches the script\'s Dylan truck; the headline is not the title and its broken grammar is a deliberate or accidental pattern-break, effect unknown.'
SCRIPT='A single-narrator list explainer built on two composite roommates (Maya and Dylan, same $52,000 start in 2010): hook (Dylan in a parking lot paying for a transmission), reframe that 22-40 dollars are the most powerful, then six killers: lifestyle creep (savings rate, $10,000 raise), cars (payments, depreciation, negative equity, $470 difference), card debt and BNPL, waiting ($500 from 25 vs 35), employer match and median balances, no emergency fund, a school-community promotion, then looking rich and overtrading (behaviour gap), a recap and the truck callback. Arithmetic largely reproduces; the saving-rate figure is stale and several survey figures are unsourced. The stored ending is truncated.'
